WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.036 --> 00:00:15.716
had a birthday—his tenth.

2
00:00:16.656 --> 00:00:17.517
Father was at work.

3
00:00:18.537 --> 00:00:22.898
But his sisters, Bobbie and Phyllis, and his mother all gave him presents in the morning.

4
00:00:24.099 --> 00:00:27.420
One of these presents was a model engine, and Peter was overjoyed.

5
00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:33.282
Peter's joy lasted for three days until the engine suddenly went bang!

6
00:00:33.922 --> 00:00:34.903
The engine was broken.

7
00:00:35.823 --> 00:00:37.064
Peter was very unhappy.

8
00:00:38.105 --> 00:00:42.107
His sisters said he had cried, but Peter insisted his eyes were red from a cold.

9
00:00:44.228 --> 00:00:47.910
When Father came home that evening, Peter told him the story of the broken engine.

10
00:00:49.571 --> 00:00:51.392
Father looked at the toy engine carefully.

11
00:00:51.412 --> 00:00:53.893
"Hmm," said Father.

12
00:00:54.893 --> 00:00:56.334
The children waited impatiently.

13
00:00:56.354 --> 00:00:58.375
"Is there any hope?"

14
00:00:58.816 --> 00:00:59.336
asked Peter.

15
00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:05.482
"Yes, it can be fixed with some tools—but not tonight," said Father cheerfully.

16
00:01:05.502 --> 00:01:09.644
"Let's wait till Saturday and you can all help me fix it."

17
00:01:11.145 --> 00:01:13.006
"Can girls help to fix engines?"

18
00:01:13.386 --> 00:01:14.427
Peter asked doubtfully.

19
00:01:14.447 --> 00:01:16.247
"Of course!

20
00:01:17.468 --> 00:01:20.449
Girls are just as clever as boys, and don't you forget it!"

21
00:01:20.749 --> 00:01:21.290
Father said.

22
00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:24.511
"How would you like to be an engine driver, Phyllis?"

23
00:01:24.531 --> 00:01:30.442
"No, my face would always be dirty," said Phyllis.

24
00:01:33.163 --> 00:01:35.404
"I would just love it," said Bobbie.

25
00:01:36.184 --> 00:01:38.765
"Can I be an engine driver when I grow up, Father?"

26
00:01:38.785 --> 00:01:41.106
"Yes, we'll help you!"

27
00:01:41.166 --> 00:01:41.887
Father replied.

28
00:01:43.107 --> 00:01:44.408
Suddenly there was a knock at the door.

29
00:01:44.428 --> 00:01:46.388
"Who's that?"

30
00:01:46.789 --> 00:01:47.309
said Father.

31
00:01:48.849 --> 00:01:51.511
Mother came in and said that two gentlemen wanted to see Father.

32
00:01:51.531 --> 00:01:54.652
"They're in the next room," she added.

33
00:01:55.624 --> 00:01:59.287
"I hope they leave soon because it's nearly the children's bedtime."

34
00:02:00.908 --> 00:02:02.489
But the visitors stayed until late.

35
00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:07.152
Mother told the children a story about a princess with green eyes.

36
00:02:08.132 --> 00:02:11.395
It was difficult for the children to listen because voices came from the next room.

37
00:02:12.395 --> 00:02:14.317
Father's voice sounded louder than usual.

38
00:02:15.277 --> 00:02:16.418
He even sounded angry.

39
00:02:20.401 --> 00:02:21.701
Ruth, the maid, came in.

40
00:02:21.721 --> 00:02:25.264
"He wants you to go in, ma'am," she said to Mother.

41
00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:27.661
"I think he's had bad news.

42
00:02:28.661 --> 00:02:29.742
Be ready for the worst."

43
00:02:31.122 --> 00:02:34.083
So Mother went into the next room, and there was more talking.

44
00:02:35.784 --> 00:02:37.925
Later Mother came back, and her face was pale.

45
00:02:37.945 --> 00:02:40.946
"It's bedtime," she said.

46
00:02:40.966 --> 00:02:42.987
"Ruth will put you to bed."

47
00:02:43.007 --> 00:02:47.469
"But you promised we could stay up with Father!"

48
00:02:47.889 --> 00:02:48.449
said Phyllis.

49
00:02:48.469 --> 00:02:52.551
"Father had to leave—on business," said Mother.

50
00:02:53.971 --> 00:02:55.412
The children kissed her and went to bed.

51
00:02:56.372 --> 00:02:57.053
Bobbie lingered.

52
00:02:58.034 --> 00:03:01.817
She hugged Mother and whispered, "It wasn't bad news, was it, Mommy?

53
00:03:02.678 --> 00:03:04.179
Did someone die?"

54
00:03:04.199 --> 00:03:10.624
"Nobody died, no," said Mother, and she almost seemed to push Bobbie away.

55
00:03:14.468 --> 00:03:17.170
When the children woke up the next morning, Mother was gone.

56
00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:23.856
"I think something awful has happened," said Peter during breakfast.

57
00:03:24.848 --> 00:03:27.589
"I asked Ruth, and she said we'll find out soon."

58
00:03:27.609 --> 00:03:30.370
"You should have waited to ask Mother!"

59
00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:31.570
Bobbie said angrily.

60
00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:35.411
It was seven o'clock in the evening when Mother came home.

61
00:03:36.411 --> 00:03:37.232
She looked worn-out.

62
00:03:38.372 --> 00:03:44.434
After she rested and had a cup of tea, she said, "My darlings, I want to tell you

63
00:03:44.514 --> 00:03:48.715
something. Those men did bring very bad news last night.

64
00:03:50.415 --> 00:03:52.156
Father won't be here for some time.

65
00:03:53.128 --> 00:03:56.113
I am very worried, and I want you to help me.

66
00:03:57.175 --> 00:04:00.280
You can help me by being good and not quarreling."

67
00:04:01.422 --> 00:04:03.345
The children wondered why Father had to leave.

68
00:04:04.346 --> 00:04:05.168
What could have happened?
